   "actionDesc": "Introduced in House",
   "text": "<p><strong>Noncontiguous Shipping Reasonable Rate Act of 2023</strong></p><p>This bill provides that a rate for service in noncontiguous domestic ocean trade  is reasonable if such rate is within 10% of a rate set by a comparable international ocean rate index recognized by the Federal Maritime Commission. (Under current law, a rate is required to be reasonable, and the Surface Transportation Board generally has the authority to determine whether certain rates are reasonable.)&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><!--tinycomments|2.1|data:application/json;base64,-->",
